{"id":"mahabharata-12-103","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":103,"title":"त्र्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 103 · Signs of victory and how to behave","summary":{"en":"Bhishma describes the signs of an army that will win, such as its good spirits, healthy omens and calm weather. He says that the king must reassure all creatures without deceit and win the hearts of the people.","kn":"ಗೆಲ್ಲುವ ಸೈನ್ಯದ ಚಿಹ್ನೆಗಳನ್ನು ಅದರ ಉತ್ಸಾಹ, ಶುಭ ಶಕುನ, ಶಾಂತ ಹವಾಮಾನದ ಮೂಲಕ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ರಾಜ ಮೋಸವಿಲ್ಲದೆ ಎಲ್ಲ ಜೀವಿಗಳಿಗೆ ಭರವಸೆ ನೀಡಿ ಪ್ರಜೆಗಳ ಹೃದಯ ಗೆಲ್ಲಬೇಕೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीष्म विजयी सेना के लक्षण बताते हैं, जैसे उसका उत्साह, शुभ शकुन और शान्त मौसम। वे कहते हैं कि राजा छल के बिना सब प्राणियों को आश्वस्त करे और प्रजा के हृदय जीते।","te":"గెలిచే సైన్యం లక్షణాలను దాని ఉత్సాహం, శుభ శకునాలు, ప్రశాంత వాతావరణం ద్వారా భీష్ముడు వర్ణిస్తాడు. రాజు మోసం లేకుండా అన్ని జీవులకు భరోసా ఇచ్చి ప్రజల హృదయాలను గెలవాలంటాడు.","ta":"வெல்லும் படையின் அடையாளங்களை அதன் உற்சாகம், நல்ல நிமித்தங்கள், அமைதியான வானிலை மூலம் பீஷ்மர் விவரிக்கிறார். மன்னன் வஞ்சகமின்றி எல்லா உயிர்களுக்கும் நம்பிக்கை அளித்து மக்களின் உள்ளத்தை வெல்ல வேண்டும் என்கிறார்.","ml":"നല്ല മനോവീര്യം, ശുഭലക്ഷണങ്ങൾ, ശാന്തമായ കാലാവസ്ഥ എന്നിങ്ങനെ വിജയിക്കുന്ന സൈന്യത്തിന്റെ ലക്ഷണങ്ങൾ ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. വഞ്ചനയില്ലാതെ എല്ലാ ജീവികൾക്കും ആശ്വാസം നൽകണമെന്നും, ജനങ്ങളുടെ ഹൃദയം നേടണമെന്നും രാജാവിനോട് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.103; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"जैत्र्या वा कानि रूपाणि भवन्ति पुरुषर्षभ ।\nपृतनायाः प्रशस्तानि तानीहेच्छामि वेदितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bull among men, what are the marks of a victorious army, the signs that are held auspicious? I wish to know them."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"जैत्र्या वा यानि रूपाणि भवन्ति पुरुषर्षभ ।\nपृतनायाः प्रशस्तानि तानि वक्ष्यामि सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bull among men, I shall tell you fully the signs that mark a victorious and praiseworthy army."}},{"n":3,"text":"दैवं पूर्वं विकुरुते मानुषे कालचोदिते ।\nतद्विद्वांसोऽनुपश्यन्ति ज्ञानदीर्घेण चक्षुषा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fate first shows itself in changes, when human affairs are driven by time; the wise see this with the long eye of knowledge."}},{"n":4,"text":"प्रायश्चित्तविधिं चात्र जपहोमांश्च तद्विदः ।\nमङ्गलानि च कुर्वन्तः शमयन्त्यहितान्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who know the rules of expiation, with prayers, fire offerings and auspicious rites, can also calm inauspicious signs."}},{"n":5,"text":"उदीर्णमनसो योधा वाहनानि च भारत ।\nयस्यां भवन्ति सेनायां ध्रुवं तस्यां जयं वदेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In whatever army the warriors and the mounts are high-spirited, Bharata, one may say victory is certain."}},{"n":6,"text":"अन्वेनां वायवो वान्ति तथैवेन्द्रधनूंषि च ।\nअनुप्लवन्ते मेघाश्च तथादित्यस्य रश्मयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When winds blow behind it, and rainbows, clouds and the sun's rays follow it..."}},{"n":7,"text":"गोमायवश्चानुलोमा वडा गृध्राश्च सर्वशः ।\nआचरेयुर्यदा सेनां तदा सिद्धिरनुत्तमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"...and when jackals, mares and vultures move all around it favourably, then success is supreme."}},{"n":8,"text":"प्रसन्नभाः पावक ऊर्ध्वरश्मिः\nप्रदक्षिणावर्तशिखो विधूमः ।\nपुण्या गन्धाश्चाहुतीनां प्रवान्ति\nजयस्यैतद्भाविनो रूपमाहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the fire is bright, with upward flames, curling to the right and smokeless, and the pure scent of oblations drifts, they say this is the sign of coming victory."}},{"n":9,"text":"गम्भीरशब्दाश्च महास्वनाश्च\nशङ्खाश्च भेर्यश्च नदन्ति यत्र ।\nयुयुत्सवश्चाप्रतीपा भवन्ति\nजयस्यैतद्भाविनो रूपमाहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where conches and kettledrums sound deep and loud, and the warriors who want to fight meet no opposition, they say this is the sign of coming victory."}},{"n":10,"text":"इष्टा मृगाः पृष्ठतो वामतश्च\nसंप्रस्थितानां च गमिष्यतां च ।\nजिघांसतां दक्षिणाः सिद्धिमाहु-\nर्ये त्वग्रतस्ते प्रतिषेधयन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deer seen behind and on the left, for those setting out or about to go, are auspicious; on the right they promise success to those who wish to kill; those that appear in front forbid it."}},{"n":11,"text":"मङ्गल्यशब्दाः शकुना वदन्ति\nहंसाः क्रौञ्चाः शतपत्राश्च चाषाः ।\nहृष्टा योधाः सत्त्ववन्तो भवन्ति\nजयस्यैतद्भाविनो रूपमाहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When birds give auspicious cries, swans, cranes, woodpeckers and chasha birds, and the warriors are glad and strong, they say this is the sign of coming victory."}},{"n":12,"text":"शस्त्रैः पत्रैः कवचैः केतुभिश्च\nसुभानुभिर्मुखवर्णैश्च यूनाम् ।\nभ्राजिष्मती दुष्प्रतिप्रेक्षणीया\nयेषां चमूस्तेऽभिभवन्ति शत्रून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those whose army blazes with weapons, banners, armour and standards and the shining faces of the young, hard to look at, overcome their enemies."}},{"n":13,"text":"शुश्रूषवश्चानभिमानिनश्च\nपरस्परं सौहृदमास्थिताश्च ।\nयेषां योधाः शौचमनुष्ठिताश्च\nजयस्यैतद्भाविनो रूपमाहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the warriors are obedient and free from conceit, have friendship with one another, and are pure in conduct, they say this is the sign of coming victory."}},{"n":14,"text":"शब्दाः स्पर्शास्तथा गन्धा विचरन्ति मनःप्रियाः ।\nधैर्यं चाविशते योधान्विजयस्य मुखं तु तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When sounds, touches and scents that please the mind are about and courage enters the warriors, that is the face of victory."}},{"n":15,"text":"इष्टो वामः प्रविष्टस्य दक्षिणः प्रविविक्षतः ।\nपश्चात्संसाधयत्यर्थं पुरस्तात्प्रतिषेधति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who enters, the left is favourable; for one about to enter, the right; behind, it brings the goal about; in front, it forbids."}},{"n":16,"text":"संभृत्य महतीं सेनां चतुरङ्गां युधिष्ठिर ।\nसाम्नैवावर्तने पूर्वं प्रयतेथास्ततो युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gathered a great army of four divisions, Yudhishthira, first try by conciliation alone to turn the foe back, and only after that fight."}},{"n":17,"text":"जघन्य एष विजयो यद्युद्धं नाम भारत ।\nयादृच्छिको युधि जयो दैवो वेति विचारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Victory by what is called war is the lowest kind, Bharata; whether victory in battle comes by chance or by fate is a matter for doubt."}},{"n":18,"text":"अपामिव महावेगस्त्रस्ता मृगगणा इव ।\nदुर्निवार्यतमा चैव प्रभग्ना महती चमूः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great army that is broken is like a great rush of waters or herds of frightened deer, and is very hard to restrain."}},{"n":19,"text":"भग्ना इत्येव भज्यन्ते विद्वांसोऽपि नकारणम् ।\nउदारसारा महती रुरुसंघोपमा चमूः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even the wise break, saying 'We are broken' without cause; a great army of noble strength is like a herd of ruru deer."}},{"n":20,"text":"परस्परज्ञाः संहृष्टास्त्यक्तप्राणाः सुनिश्चिताः ।\nअपि पञ्चाशतिः शूरा मृद्नन्ति परवाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing one another, glad, ready to die and firmly resolved, even fifty heroes can crush an enemy host."}},{"n":21,"text":"अथ वा पञ्च षट्सप्त सहिताः कृतनिश्चयाः ।\nकुलीनाः पूजिताः सम्यग्विजयन्तीह शात्रवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or five, six or seven united and resolved, of good family and well honoured, win against their enemies."}},{"n":22,"text":"संनिपातो न गन्तव्यः शक्ये सति कथंचन ।\nसान्त्वभेदप्रदानानां युद्धमुत्तरमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should never go to a clash if one can avoid it; of conciliation, division, gifts and war, war is said to come last."}},{"n":23,"text":"संसर्पणाद्धि सेनाया भयं भीरून्प्रबाधते ।\nवज्रादिव प्रज्वलितादियं क्व नु पतिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The advance of an army terrifies the timid: 'Where will this fall, like a blazing thunderbolt?'"}},{"n":24,"text":"अभिप्रयातां समितिं ज्ञात्वा ये प्रतियान्त्यथ ।\nतेषां स्पन्दन्ति गात्राणि योधानां विषयस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who march out against a force they know is advancing, their limbs and their country's warriors tremble."}},{"n":25,"text":"विषयो व्यथते राजन्सर्वः सस्थाणुजङ्गमः ।\nशस्त्रप्रतापतप्तानां मज्जा सीदति देहिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The whole land, O king, with all things standing and moving, shakes; in those scorched by the heat of weapons the very marrow sinks."}},{"n":26,"text":"तेषां सान्त्वं क्रूरमिश्रं प्रणेतव्यं पुनः पुनः ।\nसंपीड्यमाना हि परे योगमायान्ति सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Conciliation mixed with harshness should be applied to them again and again, for when pressed, enemies come to terms in every way."}},{"n":27,"text":"अन्तराणां च भेदार्थं चारानभ्यवचारयेत् ।\nयश्च तस्मात्परो राजा तेन संधिः प्रशस्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"To split their inner circle he should send out spies; and with the king beyond that one, an alliance is praised."}},{"n":28,"text":"न हि तस्यान्यथा पीडा शक्या कर्तुं तथाविधा ।\nयथा सार्धममित्रेण सर्वतः प्रतिबाधनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For his torment cannot otherwise be so effective as pressing him on every side together with an enemy."}},{"n":29,"text":"क्षमा वै साधुमाया हि न हि साध्वक्षमा सदा ।\nक्षमायाश्चाक्षमायाश्च विद्धि पार्थ प्रयोजनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Forbearance is a good man's deceit, yet a good man is not always forbearing; know, Partha, the purposes of both forbearance and its lack."}},{"n":30,"text":"विजित्य क्षममाणस्य यशो राज्ञोऽभिवर्धते ।\nमहापराधा ह्यप्यस्मिन्विश्वसन्ति हि शत्रवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who forgives after conquering gains fame, and even enemies who have done great wrong trust him."}},{"n":31,"text":"मन्यते कर्शयित्वा तु क्षमा साध्विति शम्बरः ।\nअसंतप्तं तु यद्दारु प्रत्येति प्रकृतिं पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shambara held that forbearance is good only after weakening the foe; wood that has not been heated returns to its former shape."}},{"n":32,"text":"नैतत्प्रशंसन्त्याचार्या न च साधु निदर्शनम् ।\nअक्लेशेनाविनाशेन नियन्तव्याः स्वपुत्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Teachers do not praise this, nor is it a good example; they should be restrained, without distress or destruction, like one's own sons."}},{"n":33,"text":"द्वेष्यो भवति भूतानामुग्रो राजा युधिष्ठिर ।\nमृदुमप्यवमन्यन्ते तस्मादुभयभाग्भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A harsh king, Yudhishthira, becomes hated by creatures, and a mild one is despised; so he should have a share of both."}},{"n":34,"text":"प्रहरिष्यन्प्रियं ब्रूयात्प्रहरन्नपि भारत ।\nप्रहृत्य च कृपायेत शोचन्निव रुदन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"One about to strike should speak pleasantly, and even while striking, Bharata; after striking he should show pity, as if grieving and weeping."}},{"n":35,"text":"न मे प्रियं यत्स हतः संप्राहैवं पुरो वचः ।\nन चकर्थ च मे वाक्यमुच्यमानः पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'It was not my wish that he be killed; he said so earlier, and though told again and again he did not heed me.'"}},{"n":36,"text":"अहो जीवितमाकाङ्क्षे नेदृशो वधमर्हति ।\nसुदुर्लभाः सुपुरुषाः संग्रामेष्वपलायिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Oh, I would have wished him to live; he did not deserve such a death. Good men who do not flee in battle are very rare.'"}},{"n":37,"text":"कृतं ममाप्रियं तेन येनायं निहतो मृधे ।\nइति वाचा वदन्हन्तॄन्पूजयेत रहोगतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'He did me wrong, by which he was killed in battle.' So saying, he should honour the killers in private."}},{"n":38,"text":"हन्तॄणां चाहतानां च यत्कुर्युरपराधिनः ।\nक्रोशेद्बाहुं प्रगृह्यापि चिकीर्षञ्जनसंग्रहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What the guilty do for the slayers and the slain, he should raise his arm and cry out, wishing to gather the people."}},{"n":39,"text":"एवं सर्वास्ववस्थासु सान्त्वपूर्वं समाचरन् ।\nप्रियो भवति भूतानां धर्मज्ञो वीतभीर्नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus in every circumstance, acting with conciliation first, a king who knows dharma and has no fear becomes dear to creatures."}},{"n":40,"text":"विश्वासं चात्र गच्छन्ति सर्वभूतानि भारत ।\nविश्वस्तः शक्यते भोक्तुं यथाकाममुपस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All creatures trust such a king, Bharata; a trusted man can be enjoyed as one wishes once he has come near."}},{"n":41,"text":"तस्माद्विश्वासयेद्राजा सर्वभूतान्यमायया ।\nसर्वतः परिरक्षेच्च यो महीं भोक्तुमिच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"So a king who wishes to enjoy the earth should win the trust of all creatures without deceit and guard it on every side."}}]}]}